---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { PUBLIC_SITE_URL } from 'astro:env/client';

const seoTitle = 'Comegame Bonus Guide for Indian Users: Welcome Offers, Referrals & Wagering Explained';
const seoDescription =
	'A complete guide to Comegame bonuses in India — welcome offers, referral rewards, deposit matches, wagering requirements, bonus traps, and how to claim safely.';
const canonicalUrl = `${PUBLIC_SITE_URL}/blog/comegame-bonus-guide-india`;
const ogImage = `${PUBLIC_SITE_URL}/android-chrome-512x512.png`;
const keywordsMeta =
	'comegame bonus india, come game welcome offer, comegame referral reward, comegame wagering requirements, online gaming bonus india, comegame deposit bonus, comegame promotion guide, comegame cashback';

const articleSchema = {
	'@context': 'https://schema.org',
	'@type': 'BlogPosting',
	headline: seoTitle,
	description: seoDescription,
	url: canonicalUrl,
	image: ogImage,
	datePublished: '2026-07-01',
	dateModified: '2026-07-01',
	inLanguage: 'en-IN',
	author: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'Come Game Guide' },
	publisher: {
		'@type': 'Organization',
		name: 'Come Game Guide',
		logo: { '@type': 'ImageObject', url: ogImage },
	},
	mainEntityOfPage: canonicalUrl,
};

const faqSchema = {
	'@context': 'https://schema.org',
	'@type': 'FAQPage',
	mainEntity: [
		{
			'@type': 'Question',
			name: 'What is the welcome bonus on Comegame?',
			acceptedAnswer: {
				'@type': 'Answer',
				text: 'The welcome bonus on Comegame is typically a deposit match or free credits offered to new users upon their first deposit. The exact amount and terms vary; always read the current T&Cs on the platform before claiming.',
			},
		},
		{
			'@type': 'Question',
			name: 'What are wagering requirements on Comegame?',
			acceptedAnswer: {
				'@type': 'Answer',
				text: 'Wagering requirements specify how many times you must play through the bonus amount before withdrawing any winnings derived from it. For example, a 10x wagering requirement on a ₹500 bonus means you must wager ₹5,000 before withdrawal is allowed.',
			},
		},
		{
			'@type': 'Question',
			name: 'How does the Comegame referral bonus work?',
			acceptedAnswer: {
				'@type': 'Answer',
				text: 'You share your unique referral code with a friend. When they register and complete the required actions (usually a first deposit), both you and your friend receive a reward. Check the referral section in your account for current reward amounts and conditions.',
			},
		},
		{
			'@type': 'Question',
			name: 'Can I withdraw a bonus directly on Comegame?',
			acceptedAnswer: {
				'@type': 'Answer',
				text: 'Not usually. Most bonuses on Comegame are subject to wagering requirements that must be met before the bonus-derived winnings become withdrawable. The bonus amount itself is often non-withdrawable and only the winnings from wagering it can be cashed out.',
			},
		},
		{
			'@type': 'Question',
			name: 'Are Comegame bonuses available in all Indian states?',
			acceptedAnswer: {
				'@type': 'Answer',
				text: 'Real-money gaming promotions may be restricted in certain Indian states where such activity is regulated differently. Check the platform terms and your local state regulations before claiming any real-money bonus.',
			},
		},
	],
};
---

<Layout
	title={seoTitle}
	description={seoDescription}
	keywords={keywordsMeta}
	canonical={canonicalUrl}
	ogImage={ogImage}
>
	<Fragment slot="head">
		<script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(articleSchema)}></script>
		<script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(faqSchema)}></script>
	</Fragment>

	<article class="container mx-auto px-4 py-12 md:py-16">
		<header class="max-w-4xl">
			<a href="/blog" class="inline-flex rounded-full border border-border bg-card px-3 py-1 text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wide text-muted-foreground hover:text-foreground">
				Back to Blog
			</a>
			<h1 class="mt-4 text-3xl font-black tracking-tight text-foreground md:text-5xl">
				Comegame Bonus Guide for Indian Users: Welcome Offers, Referrals &amp; Wagering Explained
			</h1>
			<p class="mt-3 text-sm font-semibold text-muted-foreground">Published on July 1, 2026 | Bonus &amp; Promotions Guide</p>
			<p class="mt-5 text-base leading-7 text-muted-foreground md:text-lg">
				Bonuses on online gaming platforms look straightforward — get extra money, play more, win more. In reality,
				the mechanics behind these offers are far more layered than the headline numbers suggest. This guide
				breaks down every type of bonus available on Comegame, explains the terms that govern each one, and
				gives Indian users a clear framework for deciding whether a particular offer is actually worth claiming.
			</p>
		</header>

		<div class="mt-8 max-w-5xl overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-border bg-card/50 p-5">
			<div class="grid items-center gap-4 md:grid-cols-[auto_1fr]">
				<img src="/logo.svg" alt="Comegame bonus guide for India" class="h-16 w-16 rounded-xl border border-border bg-background p-2" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
				<p class="text-sm leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
					Quick note: Before claiming any bonus, read the full terms on the platform. If you are new, start
					with our <a href="/blog/comegame-account-setup-guide" class="text-primary underline-offset-4 hover:underline">account setup guide</a> to
					ensure your profile is complete — incomplete KYC can block bonus withdrawals entirely. Also review the
					<a href="/responsible-gaming" class="text-primary underline-offset-4 hover:underline">responsible gaming page</a> before depositing.
				</p>
			</div>
		</div>

		<section class="mt-10 max-w-4xl rounded-xl border border-border bg-card p-6">
			<h2 class="text-2xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-foreground md:text-3xl">Why Bonuses Exist on Gaming Platforms</h2>
			<p class="mt-4 text-base leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
				Every bonus on a platform like Comegame serves a business purpose. Welcome bonuses exist to lower the
				barrier for new users to make their first deposit. Referral bonuses reduce paid acquisition costs by
				turning existing users into brand ambassadors. Deposit match bonuses keep existing users active and
				encourage top-ups. Cashback offers reduce churn by softening the sting of losses.
			</p>
			<p class="mt-4 text-base leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
				None of this means bonuses are bad for users — many genuine value opportunities exist. The key is
				understanding what you are agreeing to when you click "Claim." The platform always designs bonus
				structures to be commercially sustainable, which means the terms will favour the platform in aggregate.
				Individual users can still benefit if they approach each offer with clear eyes and read the fine print.
			</p>
			<p class="mt-4 text-base leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
				If you are curious about how the platform is structured overall, our article on
				<a href="/blog/how-online-gaming-platforms-like-comegame-operate" class="text-primary underline-offset-4 hover:underline">how online gaming platforms like Comegame operate</a>
				gives useful background on how revenue, rewards, and platform economics fit together.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="mt-8 max-w-4xl rounded-xl border border-border bg-card p-6">
			<h2 class="text-2xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-foreground md:text-3xl">Welcome Bonus: What New Users Get</h2>
			<p class="mt-4 text-base leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
				The welcome bonus is the first offer a new Comegame user encounters. It is typically structured as a
				deposit match — the platform adds a percentage of your first deposit to your bonus wallet. For example,
				a 100% match up to ₹1,000 means if you deposit ₹1,000, you receive ₹1,000 in bonus credits, bringing
				your total playable balance to ₹2,000. The headline looks attractive, but what matters more are the
				conditions attached.
			</p>
			<p class="mt-4 text-base leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
				Welcome bonuses almost always come with a minimum deposit threshold, a wagering requirement, a validity
				period, and often a list of restricted game types. A common structure might look like: 100% match up to
				₹500, with a 15x wagering requirement and a 7-day expiry. That means you need to wager ₹7,500 within
				seven days before the bonus funds become withdrawable. If you do not meet the requirement in time, the
				bonus expires and disappears.
			</p>
			<p class="mt-4 text-base leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
				Before triggering the welcome offer, complete your account setup fully. As explained in our
				<a href="/blog/comegame-account-setup-guide" class="text-primary underline-offset-4 hover:underline">Comegame account setup guide</a>,
				unverified accounts often cannot withdraw bonus winnings even after meeting wagering requirements. The
				KYC process takes time, so start it before making your first deposit.
			</p>
			<h3 class="mt-6 text-xl font-bold text-foreground">How to Evaluate a Welcome Offer</h3>
			<p class="mt-3 text-base leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
				Ask yourself four questions before claiming: What is the wagering requirement (expressed as a multiplier)?
				How many days do I have to meet it? Are there any game restrictions? What is the maximum withdrawal
				amount from bonus winnings? If a bonus has a wagering requirement above 20x, a validity of under five days,
				or restricts your preferred game types, the offer likely has more restrictions than benefits for your
				specific usage pattern.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="mt-8 max-w-4xl rounded-xl border border-border bg-card p-6">
			<h2 class="text-2xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-foreground md:text-3xl">Referral Bonuses: Earning by Inviting Friends</h2>
			<p class="mt-4 text-base leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
				Comegame's referral programme lets existing users earn rewards by inviting new players. You share your
				unique referral code or link — available in your account settings — and when a friend registers and
				completes the qualifying action (typically a first deposit), both parties receive a reward. The referrer
				might get a flat cash credit, a percentage of the new user's first deposit, or bonus credits for future
				play. The referred user usually gets an enhanced welcome offer compared to organic sign-ups.
			</p>
			<p class="mt-4 text-base leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
				Referral bonuses are among the cleaner offer types because the conditions are generally simpler than
				welcome bonus wagering structures. However, there are still terms to watch: the referred user may need
				to meet a minimum deposit, complete verification, and sometimes play a minimum number of games before
				the referral reward is credited to your account. Some platforms also cap the total number of referrals
				per user per month.
			</p>
			<p class="mt-4 text-base leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
				One important note: do not share referral links with people who are not genuinely interested in the
				platform just to collect credits. If referred accounts are flagged for inactivity or abuse, the
				platform may withhold referral rewards or restrict your account. Our
				<a href="/faq" class="text-primary underline-offset-4 hover:underline">FAQ section</a> covers
				common questions about referral eligibility and what happens if a referred user does not complete the required steps.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="mt-8 max-w-4xl rounded-xl border border-border bg-card p-6">
			<h2 class="text-2xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-foreground md:text-3xl">Deposit Bonuses and Reload Offers</h2>
			<p class="mt-4 text-base leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
				Beyond the welcome bonus, Comegame periodically offers deposit bonuses to existing users. These reload
				offers follow a similar structure to the welcome bonus — you deposit an amount and receive a percentage
				match in bonus credits. They are typically lower in value than the initial welcome offer (for example,
				a 50% match up to ₹500 on your second deposit versus a 100% match on your first).
			</p>
			<p class="mt-4 text-base leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
				Reload bonuses appear most commonly around weekends, festivals, or special events. Diwali, IPL season,
				and major tournaments often trigger promotional windows. These seasonal promotions are worth watching
				if you already use the platform regularly and were planning a deposit anyway. The key discipline: do
				not make a deposit you were not already planning just because a bonus is available. That is precisely
				the trap these promotions are designed to create.
			</p>
			<p class="mt-4 text-base leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
				For context on the broader gaming landscape and how deposit mechanics compare across platforms, see our
				<a href="/blog/comegame-vs-other-online-gaming-platforms" class="text-primary underline-offset-4 hover:underline">Comegame vs other online gaming platforms comparison</a>.
				It helps you understand whether Comegame's bonus structure is competitive relative to alternatives.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="mt-8 max-w-4xl rounded-xl border border-border bg-card p-6">
			<h2 class="text-2xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-foreground md:text-3xl">Understanding Wagering Requirements in Depth</h2>
			<p class="mt-4 text-base leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
				Wagering requirements — also called playthrough requirements — are the single most important term to
				understand before claiming any bonus. They define how much total gameplay volume you must generate
				using the bonus before the resulting winnings become withdrawable. The requirement is expressed as a
				multiplier: if you receive ₹500 in bonus credits with a 10x wagering requirement, you must wager a
				total of ₹5,000 before you can withdraw.
			</p>
			<p class="mt-4 text-base leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
				Here is where it gets subtle: "wagering" does not always mean the total amount you spend. On some
				platforms, wagering is calculated from the bonus amount only. On others, it applies to the deposit
				plus bonus combined. Read the specific language carefully. "10x on bonus" versus "10x on deposit
				plus bonus" makes an enormous practical difference. A ₹1,000 deposit with a ₹500 bonus at 10x is
				either ₹5,000 in total wagers or ₹15,000 depending on which formula applies.
			</p>
			<p class="mt-4 text-base leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
				Additionally, different games contribute differently toward wagering requirements. Skill-based games
				on Comegame often count at 100% toward wagering. However, certain game types may be excluded from
				wagering contribution entirely or count at a reduced rate (say, 50%). If you primarily play games
				with reduced contribution, your effective playthrough requirement doubles or more. This is one of
				the most overlooked details in bonus terms. Visit the
				<a href="/blog/comegame-skill-games-explained" class="text-primary underline-offset-4 hover:underline">Comegame skill games explained guide</a>
				to understand which game types exist on the platform and how they work mechanically.
			</p>
			<h3 class="mt-6 text-xl font-bold text-foreground">Realistic Wagering Example</h3>
			<p class="mt-3 text-base leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
				Suppose you deposit ₹500 and receive a 100% welcome bonus of ₹500. Your total balance is ₹1,000.
				The wagering requirement is 20x on the bonus amount: ₹500 × 20 = ₹10,000 in total wagers required.
				You have 10 days to meet this. If you play games averaging ₹50 per session, you need 200 game rounds.
				That is 20 rounds per day. For a casual player, this may be achievable. For someone playing twice a
				week, it is not. Always calculate the realistic daily play volume required before accepting.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="mt-8 max-w-4xl rounded-xl border border-border bg-card p-6">
			<h2 class="text-2xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-foreground md:text-3xl">Cashback Offers: How They Work and When They Help</h2>
			<p class="mt-4 text-base leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
				Cashback promotions refund a percentage of your net losses over a defined period — usually weekly.
				For example, a 10% weekly cashback means if you lose ₹1,000 net across the week, you receive ₹100
				back. Cashback offers are psychologically reassuring but require careful evaluation.
			</p>
			<p class="mt-4 text-base leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
				The mechanics vary significantly. Some cashback is credited directly to your withdrawable balance —
				that is the cleanest version. Others credit it as bonus money with wagering requirements attached,
				making it less immediately useful. Some cashback programmes have a cap: you may only receive cashback
				up to a maximum of ₹500 per week regardless of losses. And some have a minimum net loss threshold —
				you only qualify if your losses exceed a certain amount.
			</p>
			<p class="mt-4 text-base leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
				A genuine cashback offer with no wagering requirement on cash-credited returns is one of the most
				straightforward promotions you will find. If the cashback carries wagering, assess it the same way
				you would a deposit bonus. The underlying principle for managing all these offers responsibly is the
				same: see our <a href="/responsible-gaming" class="text-primary underline-offset-4 hover:underline">responsible gaming guidance</a>
				for how to set session and loss limits that prevent any single promotion from distorting your spending behaviour.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="mt-8 max-w-4xl rounded-xl border border-border bg-card p-6">
			<h2 class="text-2xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-foreground md:text-3xl">Seasonal Promotions and Tournament Bonuses</h2>
			<p class="mt-4 text-base leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
				Comegame, like most Indian gaming platforms, runs special promotions aligned with the Indian festival
				calendar and major sporting events. Diwali, Holi, and IPL season typically bring enhanced deposit
				matches, free entry tournaments, or doubled referral rewards. These can be genuinely valuable for
				users who are already active on the platform.
			</p>
			<p class="mt-4 text-base leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
				Tournament bonuses work slightly differently. Instead of adding to your wallet balance, they may grant
				free entries into competitive brackets with real prize pools. The skill element here is more direct —
				your performance determines your reward rather than a wagering formula. If you are already improving
				your gameplay, our guide on
				<a href="/blog/improve-performance-on-comegame-tips-guide" class="text-primary underline-offset-4 hover:underline">how to improve performance on Comegame</a>
				is worth reading before entering tournament-style events where other players have a significant head start in experience.
			</p>
			<p class="mt-4 text-base leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
				One seasonal pattern to note: promotions during high-traffic periods (major cricket matches, festive weekends)
				often come with faster expiry windows and higher wagering requirements than standard promotions, because
				the platform knows engagement is already elevated. Read terms more carefully during these periods, not
				less, even though the urgency and excitement can make it tempting to skip straight to claiming.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="mt-8 max-w-4xl rounded-xl border border-border bg-card p-6">
			<h2 class="text-2xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-foreground md:text-3xl">Common Bonus Traps and How to Avoid Them</h2>
			<p class="mt-4 text-base leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
				The term "bonus trap" refers to a situation where claiming a bonus actually makes your finances worse,
				or at best, leaves you no better off than if you had not claimed it. These situations are not always
				the result of deceptive practices — often they arise simply because users do not read the terms. Here
				are the most common patterns:
			</p>
			<ul class="mt-4 list-disc space-y-4 pl-6 text-base leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
				<li>
					<strong class="text-foreground">Deposit lock-in:</strong> Some platforms require your deposited
					funds to also meet the wagering requirement, not just the bonus amount. This means you cannot
					withdraw your own deposit until you have wagered a multiple of it. Read whether the requirement
					applies to "bonus only" or "deposit plus bonus."
				</li>
				<li>
					<strong class="text-foreground">Unrealistic wagering timelines:</strong> A 30x wagering requirement
					within 48 hours is practically impossible for most casual users. Accepting such an offer and failing
					to meet it wastes deposit money chasing an unachievable target. Calculate required daily volume before
					clicking "Claim."
				</li>
				<li>
					<strong class="text-foreground">Max bet restrictions:</strong> Some bonuses require that no single
					wager exceed a set amount (for example, ₹100 per game). Exceeding this — even once — can void
					the entire bonus. This restriction is often buried in the terms.
				</li>
				<li>
					<strong class="text-foreground">Withdrawal caps on bonus winnings:</strong> Even after meeting the
					wagering requirement, some bonuses cap how much of the resulting winnings you can withdraw. A
					₹500 bonus with a max withdrawal of ₹1,000 limits your upside regardless of performance.
				</li>
				<li>
					<strong class="text-foreground">Auto-opt-in with a deposit:</strong> On some platforms, making a
					deposit automatically opts you into a promotion unless you explicitly opt out first. If that
					promotion has restrictive terms you did not want, you may find your funds locked unexpectedly.
					Always check promotional settings before depositing.
				</li>
			</ul>
			<p class="mt-4 text-base leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
				The <a href="/real-money-come-games" class="text-primary underline-offset-4 hover:underline">real money Come Games guide</a>
				explains deposit mechanics and wallet management more broadly, which pairs well with understanding
				how bonus funds interact with your main balance. Reading both gives you a complete picture before committing money.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="mt-8 max-w-4xl rounded-xl border border-border bg-card p-6">
			<h2 class="text-2xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-foreground md:text-3xl">How to Read Bonus Terms and Conditions</h2>
			<p class="mt-4 text-base leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
				Every bonus on Comegame is governed by a set of terms and conditions. These documents are often long,
				written in dense legal language, and formatted to be skimmed rather than read. Here is a practical
				approach to reading them efficiently without missing critical details.
			</p>
			<p class="mt-4 text-base leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
				First, search or scroll to find five specific pieces of information: the wagering requirement multiplier,
				whether it applies to bonus only or deposit plus bonus, the validity period, the eligible game types,
				and whether there is a maximum withdrawal limit on bonus-derived winnings. These five variables
				determine the practical value of almost any bonus. You can usually locate them within the first few
				paragraphs of the T&amp;C if you know what to look for.
			</p>
			<p class="mt-4 text-base leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
				Second, look for exclusion clauses. Terms often specify that certain game types, payment methods, or
				user categories are ineligible. If your primary game is excluded from wagering contribution, the bonus
				has no practical value for your usage pattern regardless of how generous the headline number looks.
			</p>
			<p class="mt-4 text-base leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
				Third, note the currency treatment. Bonus credits and real money are almost always held separately in
				your wallet. Most platforms spend real money first, then bonus credits — or the reverse, depending on
				the platform design. Which balance is used first affects how quickly you clear the wagering requirement.
				If you are unsure about wallet mechanics, visit the
				<a href="/blog/comegame-withdrawal-guide" class="text-primary underline-offset-4 hover:underline">Comegame withdrawal guide</a>
				which explains how different balance types are handled during cash-out.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="mt-8 max-w-4xl rounded-xl border border-border bg-card p-6">
			<h2 class="text-2xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-foreground md:text-3xl">Loyalty Programmes and Long-Term Reward Structures</h2>
			<p class="mt-4 text-base leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
				Beyond one-time bonuses, some gaming platforms including Comegame operate tiered loyalty or VIP
				programmes. These reward consistent, high-volume play with escalating benefits: faster withdrawals,
				higher deposit match percentages, exclusive tournament invitations, or dedicated support. The higher
				your tier, the better the terms on new offers.
			</p>
			<p class="mt-4 text-base leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
				Loyalty programmes make commercial sense for dedicated players who would be using the platform heavily
				anyway. The risk is the same as any tiered programme: users may feel pressure to maintain their tier
				level, which can push them toward playing more than they would naturally. Tier maintenance requirements
				— monthly minimums of deposits or wagered amounts — should be viewed with caution. If maintaining your
				tier requires behaviour that exceeds your personal budget, step down a tier rather than stretch your
				spending. Loyalty perks should be a side benefit of natural activity, not a target that drives it.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="mt-8 max-w-4xl rounded-xl border border-border bg-card p-6">
			<h2 class="text-2xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-foreground md:text-3xl">Tax Implications of Bonus Winnings in India</h2>
			<p class="mt-4 text-base leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
				India's tax framework treats online gaming winnings distinctly. Under current rules, winnings from
				online games that exceed ₹10,000 per transaction (or in aggregate) may be subject to TDS (Tax Deducted
				at Source) at 30%. This applies to net winnings, which are calculated as total withdrawals minus total
				deposits made during a financial year.
			</p>
			<p class="mt-4 text-base leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
				The treatment of bonus-derived winnings follows the same rule — if your withdrawable winnings include
				amounts that originated from bonus credits after meeting wagering, those are still treated as winnings
				for tax purposes. The platform will typically deduct TDS at the point of withdrawal if the threshold
				is met. Keep records of your deposits, withdrawals, and any TDS certificates issued by the platform
				for your annual income tax return.
			</p>
			<p class="mt-4 text-base leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
				This is an area where Indian users frequently have questions. Our
				<a href="/faq" class="text-primary underline-offset-4 hover:underline">frequently asked questions page</a>
				covers common queries around taxes, platform compliance, and what documentation to expect. For
				personalised tax advice, consult a qualified chartered accountant — platform guides including this one
				do not constitute professional tax counsel.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="mt-8 max-w-4xl rounded-xl border border-border bg-card p-6">
			<h2 class="text-2xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-foreground md:text-3xl">Responsible Gaming and Bonuses: A Critical Note</h2>
